{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/tests/app_bundles.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T04:32:16.492724Z","id":"f816824f0af5be1cef930046e7c54d886986eafca305306caa0cce00f4bc89d9","body":{"detail":"Mutations on 8385aac40 that every test in //crates/clax-store:all still passes: removing live_artifact_in from check_bundle (crates/clax-store/src/app_bundles.rs:98), which lets a deleted artifact's surviving version gain an app_bundles row the delete trigger never removes; removing it from record_install (app_bundles.rs:347); dropping the delete_asset cleanup of a failed insert (app_bundles.rs:263-265). The soft-delete trigger is tested only on rows inserted by raw SQL (migrations.rs migration_48 test), not through put_app_bundle and delete_artifact, and the bundle's bytes going with the artifact is not checked.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":170},"content_hash":"9bc062f27028351a88d4a86e2ee5795f4a098ef755ea4d605678a8536a72cd50"},"suggested_fix":"Add: put, delete_artifact, then app_bundle is None, read_app_bundle is NotFound, and put and record_install answer NotFound.","summary":"No test puts a bundle on, or records an install of, a deleted artifact, or checks the bytes a refused insert leaves","tags":["review","test","app-push","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/tests/app_bundles.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T05:54:00.951873Z","id":"53642278816506c1016f260ee88dea2da1d4d8a70224afe4366e97baabf774b7","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a05a1fab4","summary":"tests/app_bundles.rs a_deleted_app_takes_no_bundle_or_install_and_its_bundles_go_with_it puts a bundle and an install, deletes the artifact through Store::delete_artifact, and checks the rows and bytes are gone and that a later put and record_install are refused NotFound. It fails with the live check removed from check_bundle, with it removed from record_install, and with the trigger's app_bundles delete removed. bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:all PASSED; just test-affected 6b408ac93: Executed 269 out of 324 tests: 324 tests pass. ","supersedes":"f816824f0af5be1cef930046e7c54d886986eafca305306caa0cce00f4bc89d9","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/tests/app_bundles.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T06:02:50.504120Z","id":"40cc3a0ead5dc624c4f198d322bdff4db6689b7e2b2f4e749fd9bf75e5f0840a","body":{"detail":"a_deleted_app_takes_no_bundle_or_install_and_its_bundles_go_with_it covers the live checks and the trigger. Removing the cleanup still passes every test, as on 8385aac40: nothing makes the row transaction fail after the bytes are written. A #[cfg(test)] fault point, like asset.add.write in crates/clax-store/src/assets.rs, would let a test check that the bytes are removed.","kind":"comment","references":"53642278816506c1016f260ee88dea2da1d4d8a70224afe4366e97baabf774b7","summary":"One part of f816824f stays untested: the delete_asset cleanup of a refused insert (crates/clax-store/src/app_bundles.rs, the inserted.is_err() branch of put_app_bundle_async)","tags":["review","test","app-push","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
